{
  "summary": "Expands unit test coverage for the `Sock` wrapper and platform socket API invariants across all supported operating systems. It adds tests for `Sock::Wait()` and `Sock::WaitMany()` readiness reporting matrices, multi-socket event isolation, timeout handling, non-blocking connection readiness, listening socket accept behavior, level-triggered event re-reporting, and socket options across newly created and accepted sockets.",
  "problem": "P2P and HTTP networking logic rely on platform-specific socket readiness behaviors and assumptions that were not systematically pinned down in unit tests. Gaps in test coverage allowed edge cases to go unnoticed across OS backends (such as `select()` vs `poll()` differences), contributing to bugs like CVE-2026-117350 where unexpected socket event reporting led to node out-of-memory conditions.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'This improves our `Sock` test coverage following CVE-2026-117350.'",
    "Commit ad0802789b notes critical invariants exercised: 'Only what's requested is reported (in particular, no unrequested RecvEvent when we took care not to ask for it, see CVE-2026-117350)' and 'A reported event always means we can make progress (avoid spins).'"
